---
import Solution from '../../layouts/Solution.astro';
import MinimizationFunnel from '../../components/MinimizationFunnel.astro';
import SolutionFit from '../../components/SolutionFit.astro';
import SolutionFaq from '../../components/SolutionFaq.astro';
import DocsHandoff from '../../components/DocsHandoff.astro';
import { solutionAreas } from '../../data/solutions';
import { askQuestionHref, contactEmail } from '../../data/contact';
import { products } from '../../data/products';
const area = solutionAreas.find((a) => a.key === 'check-a-fact')!;
const evidence = products.find((p) => p.key === 'evidence-gateway')!;
---
<Solution
  area={area}
  heading="Let an authorised service check a defined fact without receiving the record."
  description="Start with the decision another service must make, then define the smallest answer it needs. Evidence Gateway returns that answer from an authorised source with a digital signature, while the consuming service remains responsible for how it uses the result."
>
  <section id="example" class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="check-example-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading center">
        <p class="eyebrow">One example: a civil register</p>
        <h2 id="check-example-title">One civil register provides different permitted checks without sending the source record.</h2>
        <p>A pension service asks whether a person is recorded as alive. A licensing service asks whether an applicant meets an age threshold. The civil-registration authority defines which question each service may ask and authorises the calling service. A request outside that permission is refused.</p>
      </div>
      <MinimizationFunnel />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="check-change-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What changes for your office</p>
        <h2 id="check-change-title">Less unnecessary disclosure, with origin and integrity that the recipient can verify.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="product-facts">
        <article><h3>The receiving service gets the defined answer</h3><p>The office that keeps the register specifies what the question means and how the answer is worked out. A service can receive an age-threshold result without receiving the date of birth.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Only an authorised service can make the check</h3><p>Each connected service may ask specific questions for agreed purposes. Anything else is refused. Requests and outcomes are recorded so the registry team can review how the connection is used.</p></article>
        <article><h3>The signature proves origin and integrity</h3><p>The receiving service verifies that the answer came from the register, was not altered and is within its validity period. The signature does not prove that the source record is correct or decide what the answer means for the applicant.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <SolutionFit
    area={area}
    heading="Give a service a checked answer, or the fields it needs."
    jobs={{
      'evidence-gateway': 'Use it when another service needs a defined yes-or-no result, status or value from a declared list. It returns a digitally signed answer that the recipient can verify came from the register and was not altered.',
    }}
    extra={[
      { term: 'Your register stays where it is', body: 'Evidence Gateway works from the register your office already runs, through a connection your technical team sets up: an interface your system offers or a read-only extract your team publishes. It does not require Base Registry Engine.' },
    ]}
  >
    <p>Start from what the other service has to decide, and give it the least that decision needs. A good first question is the one your office is asked for most often.</p>
  </SolutionFit>
  <SolutionFaq
    muted
    items={[
      {
        q: 'Do we have to move our register?',
        a: 'No. Evidence Gateway reads from the register your office already runs, through a connection your technical team sets up. Your staff keep recording and correcting records where they do today, and the answers reflect what the register holds, as of the interface or extract they read.',
        link: { href: 'https://docs.registrystack.org/explanation/integration-patterns/', label: 'How it sits beside existing systems' },
      },
      {
        q: 'How does the receiving service know an answer is genuine?',
        a: 'Each answer carries a digital signature from the register that issued it and its validity period. The receiving service can verify origin and integrity itself. The signature does not prove the source data is correct or that the subject is legally entitled to something.',
        link: { href: evidence.href, label: `About ${evidence.name}` },
      },
      {
        q: 'Does this replace our data-sharing agreements?',
        a: 'No. The agreement still says what a service may know and why. The questions and fields your office sets up follow that agreement, and a request outside it is refused and kept on record.',
      },
      {
        q: 'What if the asking service uses AI?',
        a: 'It uses the same authorised connection as any other service and receives only the agreed answer. The organisation using AI remains responsible for the decision and its treatment of the person concerned. Registry Stack does not make the eligibility decision.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Where does our technical team start?',
        a: `With the ${evidence.name} tutorial, which answers a yes-or-no question from sample data and checks the answer, on a laptop.`,
        link: { href: evidence.tutorialHref, label: evidence.tutorialLabel },
      },
      {
        q: 'And if a service needs a value, not a yes or no?',
        a: 'An answer can be one of a set of values your office declares, such as the region a person lives in, and nothing outside that set. A service that needs the records themselves, such as a legal name, reads the register through the access your office grants it; Registry Stack does not publish fields from a register it does not hold.',
        link: { href: 'https://docs.registrystack.org/tutorials/return-a-governed-value/', label: 'Run the governed value tutorial' },
      },
    ]}
  />
  <DocsHandoff
    eyebrow="Work with us"
    heading="Talk it through with the people who build it."
    body="Tell us which register holds the source record, which service needs an answer and what decision that answer supports. We can help define the first question and connect both sides."
    primaryLabel="Ask a question"
    primaryHref={askQuestionHref(area.name)}
    emphasis="docs"
    note={`Or write to ${contactEmail}.`}
  />
</Solution>
